                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It is a great game. It takes a lot of time before you understand how things work. Progression is not intuitive until you fully understand. A big reason for that is it's lack of presence on the internet. Base game no mods, the progression is so tuff. More so if you build a city. It is always faster to do events and i think a ritual that triggers events in town would do a lot for towns. After fall was interesting to me as a concept, because i thought of how machines could automate the processes of gathering or crafting. To me (my only experience is thea:2) machines are the overwhelming success of dwarves and intelligence. Hacking and trickery would have been more demon like as a concept of loopholes and tricking the logic. The primary conflict would be between the nature and the crafting gods. it could have been so cool. overall thea 2: is great. I only played the demo for after fall when it came out, but it was so different, and the story didn't interest me.",
